question:
What is a memory leak in Java?
```java
List<String> cache = new ArrayList<>();
for (int i = 0; i < 1000000; i++) {
  cache.add(new String("Item " + i));
}
// cache never cleared, holds references
```

What does this code cause?
```java
int[] data = new int[1000000];
data = null;
System.out.println("Done");
```

What happens with circular references?
```java
class Node {
  Node next;
}
Node a = new Node();
Node b = new Node();
a.next = b;
b.next = a;
a = null; b = null;
```

What is the issue with this code?
```java
static List<String> cache = new ArrayList<>();
public void addToCache(String item) {
  cache.add(item);
}
```

What is a WeakReference used for?
```java
WeakReference<Object> wr = new WeakReference<>(new Object());
Object obj = wr.get();
```

What causes an OutOfMemoryError?
```java
List<int[]> list = new ArrayList<>();
while (true) {
  list.add(new int[1000000]);
}
```

What is object reachability?
```java
Object obj = new Object();
obj = null;
System.gc(); // Suggest GC
```

What does the GC do with unreachable objects?
```java
List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
list.add("item");
list.clear();
list = null;
```

What prevents GC of an object?
```java
class Listener {
  public void onEvent() { }
}
ListListener listener = new Listener();
button.addEventListener(listener);
listener = null; // Does this allow GC?
```
